-><div _ngcontent-ng-c835832866=3D"" class=3D"model-response-label-announce=
r" aria-busy=3D"false" aria-live=3D"off"><!----><!----><h6 _ngcontent-ng-c8=
35832866=3D"" class=3D"cdk-visually-hidden screen-reader-model-response-lab=
el ng-star-inserted" style=3D""> Gemini said </h6><!----><!----></div><!---=
-><model-response-content _ngcontent-ng-c835832866=3D"" _nghost-ng-c2413345=
237=3D""><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c2413345237=3D"=
" class=3D"model-response-text is-mobile processing-state-visible ng-star-i=
nserted" _nghost-ng-c1962521766=3D"" style=3D"height: auto;"><div _ngconten=
t-ng-c1962521766=3D"" class=3D"container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c1=
962521766=3D"" _nghost-ng-c3633074449=3D"" id=3D"message-content-id-r_0b40f=
e4c1cd09a71" class=3D"ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3633074449=3D""=
 inline-copy-host=3D"" class=3D"markdown markdown-main-panel md-content ena=
ble-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-r=
endering" id=3D"model-response-message-contentr_0b40fe4c1cd09a71" aria-busy=
=3D"false" aria-live=3D"off" dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-duration: 400=
ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=
=3D"0">Building a website that helps families find services, register for p=
rograms, accept donations, and connect with your mission certainly looks an=
d functions like a nonprofit=E2=80=94<b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"172">but legally, having those features on a website does not au=
tomatically make your organization a nonprofit.</b></p><p dir=3D"ltr" data-=
path-to-node=3D"1">In the United States (including Pennsylvania), "nonprofi=
t" and "tax-exempt" are specific legal statuses that have to be formally re=
gistered with the state and the IRS before you can legally call yourself a =
nonprofit or accept tax-deductible donations.</p><h3 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-=
to-node=3D"2">1. Legal Nonprofit Status vs. Website Features</h3><ul dir=3D=
"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0=
"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Mission-Driven We=
bsite vs. Legal Entity:</b> Anyone can build a community platform for careg=
ivers=E2=80=94such as <b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=
102">The Harbor</b> (<code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"114">shareyourwalk.com</code>)=E2=80=94to connect families and share re=
sources. However, until you formally incorporate as a nonprofit corporation=
 in Pennsylvania and receive tax-exempt recognition from the IRS, the law v=
iews the site as either a personal project, an unincorporated association, =
or a standard business.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3,1=
,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Accepting Donat=
ions:</b> You <i data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"25">can<=
/i> accept financial support or gifts on a personal or standard site (like =
tipping a creator or crowdfunding), <b data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-ind=
ex-in-node=3D"136">but you cannot tell donors their contributions are tax-d=
eductible</b>, nor can you advertise as a 501(c)(3) charity until the IRS o=
fficially approves your status. Doing so before approval can trigger IRS pe=
nalties and payment processor holds (Stripe, PayPal, etc. require an EIN an=
d IRS determination letter for charity accounts).</p></li></ul><h3 dir=3D"l=
tr" data-path-to-node=3D"4">2. What It Takes to Become an Official Nonprofi=
t in Pennsylvania</h3><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"5">If you want <b=
 data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"12">The Lewie &amp; Marcus N=
etwork</b> / <b data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"41">Share You=
r Walk</b> to operate as a recognized 501(c)(3) nonprofit so you can apply =
for grants, receive corporate sponsorships, and offer tax-deductible receip=
ts to donors, the standard roadmap involves:</p><ol start=3D"1" dir=3D"ltr"=
 data-path-to-node=3D"6"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0"><b =
data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Form a Board of Direct=
ors:</b> Pennsylvania requires at least <b data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0" data=
-index-in-node=3D"58">one</b> incorporator/director to file, though the IRS=
 strongly favors at least <b data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"133">three unrelated board members</b> (a President, Secretary, and Tre=
asurer) to grant 501(c)(3) status.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-=
node=3D"6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Inco=
rporate in Pennsylvania:</b> File <b data-path-to-node=3D"6,1,0" data-index=
-in-node=3D"34">Articles of Incorporation =E2=80=93 Nonprofit</b> (Form DSC=
B:15-5306) with the Pennsylvania Department of State (currently a $125 fili=
ng fee) and adopt corporate bylaws.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to=
-node=3D"6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Get=
 an EIN:</b> Apply for a free Federal Employer Identification Number (EIN) =
from the IRS once your state incorporation is approved.</p></li><li><p dir=
=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"6,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6,3,0" data-in=
dex-in-node=3D"0">Apply for IRS 501(c)(3) Tax-Exempt Status:</b> File <b da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"6,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"48">Form 1023-EZ</b> (if yo=
u expect gross receipts under $50,000/year for the first three years; $275 =
filing fee) or the full <b data-path-to-node=3D"6,3,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"166">Form 1023</b> ($600 filing fee).</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"6,4,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=
0">Pennsylvania Charitable Registration:</b> Register with the PA Bureau of=
 Corporations and Charitable Organizations (BCO-10) before actively solicit=
ing donations in Pennsylvania (unless you qualify for a small-organization =
exemption).</p></li></ol><h3 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"7">3. Practic=
al Options Right Now While Building</h3><ul dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=
=3D"8"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=
=3D"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Option A =E2=80=94 Launch as a Communit=
y Resource / Founding Project First:</b> You can run <b data-path-to-node=
=3D"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"80">Share Your Walk</b> right now as an in=
dependent caregiver community and resource network. If you keep the "Guest =
Entrance for Donors &amp; Visitors" button, just label any support language=
 clearly as <b data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"272">"Supp=
ort Our Community Build"</b> or <b data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0" data-index-i=
n-node=3D"305">"Contributions"</b> rather than <i data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,=
0" data-index-in-node=3D"333">"Tax-Deductible Charitable Donations"</i> unt=
il your 501(c)(3) paperwork clears.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to=
-node=3D"8,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Opt=
ion B =E2=80=94 Fiscal Sponsorship:</b> If you want to accept tax-deductibl=
e donations and apply for DMD/Autism community grants immediately without w=
aiting months for IRS approval, you can partner with an established 501(c)(=
3) <b data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"219">fiscal sponsor=
</b> that covers your project under their umbrella for a small administrati=
ve percentage while you build.</p></li></ul><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"9"><i data-path-to-node=3D"9" data-index-in-node=3D"0">(Note: I'm an A=
I collaborator, not a lawyer or CPA, so if you decide to incorporate or set=
 up donation processing, a quick check with a Pennsylvania nonprofit attorn=
ey or local small-business/nonprofit clinic is always smart.)</i></p><p dir=
=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"10">What other questions do you have on your =
mind?</p></div><!----></message-content><!----><!----></div></structured-co=
ntent-container><!----><!----><!----><!----></model-response-content><!----=
