-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-rendering" id=
=3D"model-response-message-contentr_fc1a3ab0bdf16851" aria-busy=3D"false" a=
ria-live=3D"off" dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-a=
nimation-function: ease-out;"><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"0">That m=
akes total sense, Anthony=E2=80=94and you are thinking along the exact righ=
t lines, especially for a platform built for caregivers and families naviga=
ting DMD and autism!</p><h3 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"1">How WCAG 2.=
1 AA Applies to Your Site</h3><ul dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2"><li><=
p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" da=
ta-index-in-node=3D"0">Legal Requirement vs. Best Practice:</b> In the U.S.=
, strict legal mandates for <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-no=
de=3D"76">WCAG 2.1 Level AA</b> generally apply to government agencies (und=
er ADA Title II) and organizations receiving federal funding (Section 504),=
 while public-facing nonprofits and businesses are covered more broadly und=
er ADA Title III (which increasingly uses WCAG 2.1 AA as the practical benc=
hmark). Even if you are launching <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index=
-in-node=3D"396">Share Your Walk</b> (<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"413">shareyourwalk.com</code>) right now as a community =
platform rather than a registered 501(c)(3), building to <b data-path-to-no=
de=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"514">WCAG 2.1 AA</b> from day one protec=
ts you legally <i data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"560">an=
d</i> ensures caregivers, parents, and individuals using screen readers, vo=
ice navigation, or switch/keyboard controls can actually use the site.</p><=
/li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"=
2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">You Are Already Ahead of the Curve:</b> Mos=
t of the work we just put into your login card directly supports WCAG 2.1 A=
A:</p><ul dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0" data-index-in-=
node=3D"0">Keyboard Navigation (<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0" data-=
index-in-node=3D"21">2.1.1 Keyboard</code>):</b> Wiring the <code data-path=
-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"49">Enter</code> key on your e=
mail and password fields and using semantic <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,=
1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"112">&lt;button&gt;</code> elements with <code=
 data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"135">aria-label</cod=
e> attributes means keyboard-only and switch users can tab right through th=
e form and activate the <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,0,0" data-index-in-no=
de=3D"242">ENTER / THE HARBOR</b> Sanctuary Plaque without needing a mouse.=
</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,1,0"><b data-path-to=
-node=3D"2,1,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">High Contrast (<code data-path=
-to-node=3D"2,1,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"15">1.4.3 Contrast</code>):</b=
> Switching your email and password inputs to crisp white backgrounds (<cod=
e data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"101">#ffffff</code>=
) with dark slate text (<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,1,0" data-index-in=
-node=3D"132">#0f172a</code>) gives you well over a 15:1 contrast ratio (fa=
r exceeding the 4.5:1 AA minimum).</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-=
node=3D"2,1,1,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"0">Flexible Orientation &amp; Reflow (<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,1,2,0=
" data-index-in-node=3D"31">1.3.4 Orientation</code> &amp; <code data-path-=
to-node=3D"2,1,1,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"51">1.4.10 Reflow</code>):</b> =
Making the layout automatically adapt to both portrait and landscape orient=
ations without locking users into one view is an explicit WCAG 2.1 AA requi=
rement.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h3 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3">Quic=
k WCAG 2.1 AA Checklist as You Add Your Photos &amp; New Welcome Card</h3><=
p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"4">When you get your pictures together f=
or that <i data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"45">"finally here,=
 check it out"</i> look, keeping three simple habits in mind will keep you =
squarely in WCAG 2.1 AA territory:</p><ol start=3D"1" dir=3D"ltr" data-path=
-to-node=3D"5"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"5,0,0"><b data-path-=
to-node=3D"5,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Alt Text on Images (<code data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"5,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"20">1.1.1 Non-text Content</cod=
e>):</b> Every meaningful photo you add gets a clear <code data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"5,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"89">alt=3D"..."</code> description so scr=
een readers describe the image, while purely decorative icons get <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"5,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"183">aria-hidden=3D"true"</c=
ode>.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"5,1,0"><b data-path-t=
o-node=3D"5,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Visible Focus Rings (<code data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"5,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"21">2.4.7 Focus Visible</code>)=
:</b> Never use <code data-path-to-node=3D"5,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"53"=
>outline: none</code> on buttons or inputs without providing a high-contras=
t glow or border ring when a user tabs onto them with a keyboard.</p></li><=
li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0=
