ntent enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-m=
arkdown-rendering" id=3D"model-response-message-contentr_7243dee884e86124" =
aria-busy=3D"false" aria-live=3D"off" dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-dura=
tion: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path=
-to-node=3D"0">While I can search, read, draft, and archive messages in you=
r Gmail, I can't create folders (labels) or set up automatic routing filter=
s for you directly. However, you can set up a Gmail filter in about 30 seco=
nds so every email tied to <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"237">The Harbor</b> (<code data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"2=
49">shareyourwalk.com</code>) automatically skips your main inbox (or stays=
 visible) and lands cleanly inside its own <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-=
index-in-node=3D"356">The Harbor</b> label!</p><h3 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to=
-node=3D"1">Set Up an Auto-Routing Filter in Gmail (Desktop / Chromebook)</=
h3><ol start=3D"1" dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"0">Open Gmail</b> on your Chromebook (<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0=
" data-index-in-node=3D"31">mail.google.com</code>).</p></li><li><p dir=3D"=
ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">Click the "Show search options" icon</b> (the three horizonta=
l slider lines on the far right side of the Gmail search bar at the top).</=
p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=
=3D"2,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Enter your filter criteria:</b></p><ul =
dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"2,2,1,0,0">In the <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,0,0" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"7">Has the words</b> field, type:
<code data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"34">"shareyourw=
alk.com" OR "The Harbor" OR "The Lewie &amp; Marcus Network"</code></p></li=
><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,1,0"><i data-path-to-node=3D=
"2,2,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">(Optional: If you are using a specific=
 sender address like <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,1,0" data-index-in-no=
de=3D"59">noreply@shareyourwalk.com</code> or <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,=
2,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"88">support@shareyourwalk.com</code>, you ca=
n put <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"127">shar=
eyourwalk.com</code> in the <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,1,1,0" data-index-i=
n-node=3D"152">From</b> field instead, or keep it in <b data-path-to-node=
=3D"2,2,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"186">Has the words</b> so it catches b=
oth incoming inquiries and outgoing/Supabase notifications.)</i></p></li></=
ul></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=
=3D"2,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Click "Create filter"</b> at the bottom=
 right of that search box.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"=
2,4,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Choose what =
happens to those emails:</b></p><ul dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1"=
><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,0,0">Check <b data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"2,4,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"6">Apply the label</b> =E2=86=92 cl=
ick <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"30">Choose lab=
el...</b> =E2=86=92 <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"48">New label...</b> =E2=86=92 type <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,0,0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"68"><code data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,0,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"68">The Harbor</code></b> and click <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,=
1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"89">Create</b>.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,1,0"><i data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,1,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">(Optional)</i> Check <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,1,0" data-=
index-in-node=3D"17">Skip the Inbox (Archive it)</b> if you want them to go=
 <i data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"68">straight</i> =
into <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"82">The Harbo=
r</b> folder on the left sidebar without cluttering your main inbox, or lea=
ve it unchecked if you want them in both places.</p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr"=
 data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,2,0"><i data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,2,0" data-in=
dex-in-node=3D"0">(Optional)</i> Check <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,2,0" d=
ata-index-in-node=3D"17">Also apply filter to matching conversations</b> at=
 the bottom so any existing emails from <b data-path-to-node=3D"2,4,1,2,0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"103">The Harbor</b> move into that label immediately.=
</p></li></ul></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,5,0"><b data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"2,5,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Click "Create filter"</b> to=
 save it.</p></li></ol><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3">From that poi=
nt on, every notification, caregiver signup, or message mentioning <b data-=
path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"80">The Harbor</b> or <code data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"94">shareyourwalk.com</code> will a=
utomatically be tagged and organized under <b data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-=
index-in-node=3D"161">The Harbor</b> on your left Gmail sidebar!</p><p dir=
=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"4">Let me know if you want to set up any sub-=
labels (like <code data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"55">The Ha=
rbor / Donations</code> or <code data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=
=3D"81">The Harbor / Support</code>) or whenever you're ready to drop your =
background photos into <code data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"=
