aptured in natural, slightly soft indoor home lighting with subtle film gra=
in. The laptop sits on a natural wooden table, with household elements soft=
ly out of focus in the background.

The web page on the screen is &quot;The Harbor&quot; (shareyourwalk.com). M=
ost of the screen is filled with a dense, natural collage of candid caregiv=
er moments acting as a background, featuring the six images we have discuss=
ed:
- Image 9: A fatigued mother sitting at a table while a young boy plays dis=
ruptively in the background.
- Image 10: A caregiver gently helping an individual with a disability tran=
sfer from a wheelchair to a bed.
- Image 11: A mother comforting a sick child over a container in a dim, clu=
ttered bedroom.
- Image 12: A caregiver tiredly driving a car packed with supplies during a=
 long-distance road trip.
- Image 16: An inspiring typography piece over ocean waves that reads &quot=
;To every autism parent who has cried in the car... YOU'RE DOING AMAZING!&q=
uot;
- Image 17: Two supportive caregivers assisting a young boy as he works wit=
h colorful tactile therapy discs on a padded table.

Superimposed in the center is a translucent &quot;frosted-glass&quot; login=
 card with soft rounded corners and a delicate white-glowing border. The ba=
ckdrop behind it is heavily blurred and semi-transparent, allowing the shap=
es and colors of the collage to filter through while keeping the card conte=
nt readable:
- At the top: Bold white &quot;MEMBER LOGIN&quot; with &quot;The Harbor&quo=
t; subtitle.
- Form Inputs: White &quot;Member Email&quot; and &quot;Password&quot; fiel=
ds, one featuring a &quot;Show&quot; button.
- Row below the inputs: &quot;Remember Me&quot; checkbox on the left, &quot=
;Forgot password?&quot; and &quot;Not a member? Click here&quot; text on th=
e right.
- Focus: A dark navy/teal &quot;ENTER THE HARBOR&quot; Sanctuary Plaque but=
ton at the bottom, centered above &quot;The Lewie &amp; Marcus Network&quot=
; tag flanked by tiny red and blue dots.

This is a cinematic, real-world glimpse of the application's portal, presen=
ting the raw, warm &quot;collage wall&quot; through a frosted-glass overlay=
