0" class=3D"first-token" style=3D"--animation-duration: 600ms;"><span class=
=3D"">Ah,</span><span> you're talking about the free-tier sleep issue on Re=
nder where the web app spins down after a period of inactivity,</span><span=
> causing that frustrating initial delay when someone first visits </span><=
b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"185">The Harbor</b><span> (=
</span><code data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"197">shareyourwa=
lk.com</code><span>)!</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"1"><spa=
n>Usually,</span><span> people set up a free external ping service (like Up=
timeRobot or Cron-job.</span><span>org) to ping their Render URL every 5 to=
 14 minutes to keep it awake.</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D=
"2"><span>Let's check why yours might not be keeping it warm:</span></p><ol=
 start=3D"1" dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0=
">What URL are you pointing the pinger to?</b><span>
Make sure the monitoring tool is pinging your exact live web address:</span=
><span> </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"111"><c=
ode data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"111">[https://the-har=
bor.onrender.com](https://the-harbor.onrender.com)</code></b><span> (or you=
r custom domain </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"201"><code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"201">[https:/=
/www.shareyourwalk.com](https://www.shareyourwalk.com)</code></b><span>) ra=
ther than the local </span><code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-=
node=3D"287">127.0.0.1</code><span> address.</span><span> If it tries to pi=
ng </span><code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"326">loca=
lhost</code><span>,</span><span> it won't see your cloud server at all!</sp=
an></p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0"><b data-path-to-=
node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Check the Ping Frequency:</b><span>
Free tiers on services like UptimeRobot work well if set to check every 5 o=
r 10 minutes.</span></p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3,2,0"=
><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Is the Monitor Act=
ive?</b><span>
Sometimes external monitors get paused or require you to verify the HTTP st=
atus check (making sure it looks for a </span><code data-path-to-node=3D"3,=
2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"137">200 OK</code><span> response from your Flas=
k app).</span></p></li></ol><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"4"><span>Ar=
e you using a service like UptimeRobot for this,</span><span> or did you tr=
y a different method to set up the ping?</span><span> Let me know and we'll=
