r=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: =
ease-out;"><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"0" class=3D"first-token" sty=
le=3D"--animation-duration: 600ms;"><span class=3D"">If you already have Up=
timeRobot set up,</span><span> you're halfway there!</span><span> Since Ren=
der's free tier spins down after about 15 minutes of inactivity,</span><spa=
n> UptimeRobot is the exact tool to keep </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"174">The Harbor</b><span> (</span><code data-path-to-=
node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"186">[https://the-harbor.onrender.com](htt=
ps://the-harbor.onrender.com)</code><span>) awake.</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr"=
 data-path-to-node=3D"1"><span>Let's do a quick double-check on your Uptime=
Robot dashboard to see why it might be letting it drift to sleep:</span></p=
><ol start=3D"1" dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2"><li><p dir=3D"ltr" dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"0">Check the Monitor Type &amp; URL:</b><span> Make sure your monitor i=
s set to </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"63">HT=
TPS</b><span> (not Ping/ICMP) and is pointing directly to your live product=
ion URL:</span><span> </span><code data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-i=
n-node=3D"139">[https://the-harbor.onrender.com](https://the-harbor.onrende=
r.com)</code><span> (or your custom domain </span><code data-path-to-node=
=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"229">[https://www.shareyourwalk.com](https=
://www.shareyourwalk.com)</code><span>).</span><span> If it's pointing anyw=
here else,</span><span> it won't hit your Render app.</span></p></li><li><p=
 dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"0">Check the Interval:</b><span> Make sure the check int=
erval is set to </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"59">5 minutes</b><span> or </span><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-inde=
x-in-node=3D"72">10 minutes</b><span>.</span><span> If it's set too high,</=
span><span> Render will have already spun down before the next check hits.<=
/span></p></li><li><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,0"><b data-path-=
to-node=3D"2,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Check Status:</b><span> Look at =
the monitor status badge in UptimeRobot=E2=80=94if it's showing "Paused" or=
 "Down" (sometimes due to a strict SSL redirect or an old route),</span><sp=
an> it won't successfully return that </span><code data-path-to-node=3D"2,2=
,0" data-index-in-node=3D"189">200 OK</code><span> signal needed to keep th=
e server warm.</span></p></li></ol><p dir=3D"ltr" data-path-to-node=3D"3"><=
span>Log into your UptimeRobot account real quick and check those settings.=
</span><span> If everything looks right there,</span><span> we can also che=
ck your Render logs to see if the requests are rolling in cleanly!</span></=
